--TEST--
`Core\Task::map` and `Core\Task::all` are two jobs, not two spellings of one: a shape literal is not an `array` and an array literal is not a written-out shape — `rule:concurrency/all-answers-a-typed-shape` and `rule:concurrency/map-preserves-keys-and-order`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// § 2: "a shape literal cannot express *one per element of a runtime array*
// and an array cannot carry a per-element type". That is the argument for two
// members rather than one, and this case is the argument stated as a pair of
// refusals — each member handed the other's subject.
//
// Both refusals are the same assignability failure, written against two
// different parameters: `map` wants an `array<T>` and `all` wants a shape
// whose every field is a callable (`CoreTy::ShapeOfCallables`). Neither
// member reaches for a diagnostic of its own — the subject is a type
// question, and the expected type is what the message names.
class Probe {
    public static function subjects(): void {
        var $a = Core\Task::map({rows: fn(): int => 1}, fn(int $n): int => $n);
        var $b = Core\Task::all([fn(): int => 1]);
        echo 1;
    }
}

Probe::subjects();
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0401]: expected `array<int>`, found `{rows: callable(): int}`
   --> case.nvs:14:33
%A
error[E0401]: expected `{name: callable(): T, ...}`, found `array<mixed>`
   --> case.nvs:15:33
%A
error: aborting due to 2 errors
